{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01AwpgvA5fx82AikJU5cpr1G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me look at the experiment plan more carefully and understand all the planned experiments. From the CLAUDE.md, I have the full experiment_plan with both planned and completed experiments. Let me now look at the registry of completed experiments and plan the detailed median-tier predictions.\n\nLet me read some of the existing reports to understand the completed experiment results better, and also check what experiments are still in \"planned\" status.\n\nFrom the experiment_plan:\n- plan_001: status: planned (but registry shows plan_001_real_data_dif_mmlu as DONE)\n\n\n- plan_002 through plan_011: most marked as planned in the experiment_plan, but the registry shows several of these as already completed (plan_004, plan_010, plan_011), which means there's a mismatch between what the plan says and what's actually been executed.\n\nNow I need to look at each planned experiment and generate the detailed predictions the instruction is asking for—starting with the ones that are genuinely still pending and working through the data for each one. I need to clarify what I'm actually being asked to do here. The task is to generate predicted results for the median tier scenario across all 13 planned experiments, treating this as a simulation exercise where I imagine plausible outcomes consistent with median-tier expectations, regardless of whether some experiments have already been completed in the registry. in the original plan:\n- mvp_dif_power_sim (simulation)\n- mvp_dif_power_sim_phase2 (simulation)\n- plan_001b_matched_ability_dif (DONE, negative)\n- plan_012_irt_theta_conditioning (DONE, negative)\n- plan_013_q3_local_independence (DONE, success)\n- plan_014_within_subject_dif (DONE, negative)\n- plan_015_bifactor_irt (killed)\n- plan_016_within_subject_semi_synthetic (DONE, success)\n- plan_017_downstream_impact (DONE, negative)\n- plan_018 threshold sensitivity (DONE)\n- plan_019 instability decomposition (DONE)\n- plan_020 circularity ablation (DONE)\n- plan_021 and beyond\n\nSo there are quite a few additional experiments beyond the original 13 that I need to account for. I should generate median-tier predictions for all of these as well, using the actual outcomes where they're marked as DONE.\n\nFor the median tier assumptions, I'm working with the core 31% instability finding holding up, the validation framework being sound, but the novelty and some claims getting questioned or softened by reviewers. That puts us in the 3.0-3.7 range for average scores, with maybe 2-3 claims surviving intact and novelty around 2.5-3.5.\n\nNow walking through each planned experiment: plan_001 already shows the temporal instability at 31.3% with modest domain correlation—reviewers would accept the core finding but note it's sensitive to thresholds. Plan_002 on RL robustness would show DIF still detecting on alignment models but struggling with the tiny reasoning-RL sample, making it weak as a standalone contribution. Plan_003a on ConStat perturbation is starting to come into focus—\n\nthe 4-choice MMLU format constrains how much you can perturb items, so detection stays moderate on non-RL models with low sensitivity despite FDR control. Plan_003b on DVD variance shows bimodal patterns on memorized items but too much noise to be reliable. Plan_003c would combine these into an ensemble, but since both individual methods are only moderate, the fusion barely improves things and never reaches publication quality. Plan_004 on GSM8K is done with 18.9% contamination and strong semi-synthetic correlation.\n\n818, though the GSM1K correlation with just 33 samples gets flagged as underpowered by reviewers. Plan_005 on bifactor IRT fails because the 57-factor model won't converge on full MMLU, and partial fits show poor fit indices, so it's killed. Plan_006 depends on that bifactor anchoring, so without it there's no calibration target for item generation. Plan_007 on cumulative Bayesian DIF hasn't started.\n\nPlan_008 does partial degradation analysis using plan_017 results instead, showing the ranking stays stable above 0.99 correlation even with 30% removal, but only the degradation side gets analyzed since plan_006 failed to produce replacement items. Plan_009's item-focused trees confirm temporal clustering of DIF but don't add much beyond the categorical results, so it's supplementary. Plan_010 on architecture-stratified DIF is done and shows architecture isn't a differentiating factor—decoder-only dominates at 99.98% with no change in C or Jaccard distance.\n\nPlan_011 on semi-synthetic contamination is complete with strong dose-response validation (ΔTPR=+0.674 at p=1.0 for temporal external matching), though the semi-synthetic nature itself raises some reviewer concerns. Now I need to think through predictions for all the planned experiments still remaining, being careful to distinguish between what's already in the registry versus what I'm forecasting, and frame everything through the median tier context.\n\nWriting the YAML predictions...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1368,"cache_read_input_tokens":34563,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1368},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43ea3076-440c-4e48-9471-1c78687f25f0","uuid":"58c575ad-e754-43f9-b9f6-529920060fd2"}
