{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012fEs5LrKwN2SwJjoSN54e3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan 019: Instability Decomposition Report\n2\t\n3\t## Research Question\n4\t\n5\tHow much of the 31.3% DIF Category C rate in temporal MH-DIF analysis is attributable to\n6\tdomain-level capability improvement (2024 models systematically outperforming 2023 models\n7\tin certain subjects) versus residual measurement instability?\n8\t\n9\t## Method\n10\t\n11\t1. **Subject accuracy delta**: For each of 57 MMLU subjects, computed the mean accuracy\n12\t   difference between focal (2024, N=807) and reference (2023, N=1080) cohorts.\n13\t2. **Logistic regression**: Predicted item-level DIF C flag (1/0) from subject-level\n14\t   accuracy delta, with and without item-level controls (CTT difficulty, discrimination).\n15\t3. **Counterfactual**: Set subject_acc_delta = 0 and re-predicted C rates to estimate\n16\t   how much DIF C would remain absent domain-level improvement.\n17\t\n18\t## Subject Accuracy Deltas\n19\t\n20\t| Statistic | Value |\n21\t|-----------|-------|\n22\t| Mean Δ    | 0.0264 |\n23\t| SD        | 0.0146 |\n24\t| Min       | -0.0087 |\n25\t| Max       | 0.0571 |\n26\t\n27\t## Logistic Regression Results\n28\t\n29\t### Model 1: DIF_C ~ subject_acc_delta\n30\t\n31\t| Variable | Coef | SE | z | p | OR (per 0.10) |\n32\t|----------|------|----|---|---|----------------|\n33\t| const | -0.8975 | 0.0400 | -22.43 | 0.0000 | — |\n34\t| subject_acc_delta | 4.3928 | 1.3602 | 3.23 | 0.0012 | 1.552 |\n35\t\n36\t- Pseudo R² = 0.0007\n37\t- AIC = 15545.2\n38\t\n39\t### Model 2: DIF_C ~ subject_acc_delta + ctt_difficulty + ctt_discrimination\n40\t\n41\t| Variable | Coef | SE | z | p |\n42\t|----------|------|----|---|---|\n43\t| const | 0.0691 | 0.0650 | 1.06 | 0.2877 |\n44\t| subject_acc_delta | -3.0972 | 1.4305 | -2.17 | 0.0304 |\n45\t| ctt_difficulty | -2.5435 | 0.1151 | -22.09 | 0.0000 |\n46\t| ctt_discrimination | 4.1155 | 0.1929 | 21.33 | 0.0000 |\n47\t\n48\t- Pseudo R² = 0.0423\n49\t- AIC = 14902.3\n50\t\n51\t## Counterfactual Analysis\n52\t\n53\t| Metric | Model 1 | Model 2 |\n54\t|--------|---------|---------|\n55\t| Predicted C% (actual) | 31.3% | 31.3% |\n56\t| Predicted C% (Δ=0) | 29.0% | 33.0% |\n57\t| Reduction | 2.4 pp | -1.6 pp |\n58\t| % of C explained | 7.6% | -5.3% |\n59\t\n60\t## Subject-Level Correlation\n61\t\n62\t| Metric | Value |\n63\t|--------|-------|\n64\t| Pearson r | 0.338 (p = 0.0101) |\n65\t| Spearman ρ | 0.307 (p = 0.0201) |\n66\t\n67\t![Subject Delta vs C%](fig_subject_delta_vs_cpct.png)\n68\t\n69\t## Decomposition Summary\n70\t\n71\t- **Total observed C%**: 31.3%\n72\t- **Model 1 (unadjusted)**: Domain improvement accounts for 2.4 pp (7.6% of total)\n73\t- **Model 2 (adjusted for item properties)**: Domain improvement accounts for -1.6 pp — coefficient reverses sign after controlling for difficulty and discrimination\n74\t\n75\t## Interpretation\n76\t\n77\tTwo findings emerge from this decomposition:\n78\t\n79\t**1. Subject-level capability improvement is a weak predictor of DIF C flags.** Model 1 (pseudo R² = 0.0007) shows a statistically significant but negligible relationship: subjects where 2024 models improved more do show slightly more DIF C items (OR = 1.55 per 10pp improvement, p = 0.0012). However, this explains only 2.4 pp of the 31.3% C rate.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43ea3076-440c-4e48-9471-1c78687f25f0","uuid":"a473d9ba-6011-40a3-8413-be89c179a88f","timestamp":"2026-05-21T09:07:43.972Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/plan_019/report/instability_decomposition_report.md","content":"# Plan 019: Instability Decomposition Report\n\n## Research Question\n\nHow much of the 31.3% DIF Category C rate in temporal MH-DIF analysis is attributable to\ndomain-level capability improvement (2024 models systematically outperforming 2023 models\nin certain subjects) versus residual measurement instability?\n\n## Method\n\n1. **Subject accuracy delta**: For each of 57 MMLU subjects, computed the mean accuracy\n   difference between focal (2024, N=807) and reference (2023, N=1080) cohorts.\n2. **Logistic regression**: Predicted item-level DIF C flag (1/0) from subject-level\n   accuracy delta, with and without item-level controls (CTT difficulty, discrimination).\n3. **Counterfactual**: Set subject_acc_delta = 0 and re-predicted C rates to estimate\n   how much DIF C would remain absent domain-level improvement.\n\n## Subject Accuracy Deltas\n\n| Statistic | Value |\n|-----------|-------|\n| Mean Δ    | 0.0264 |\n| SD        | 0.0146 |\n| Min       | -0.0087 |\n| Max       | 0.0571 |\n\n## Logistic Regression Results\n\n### Model 1: DIF_C ~ subject_acc_delta\n\n| Variable | Coef | SE | z | p | OR (per 0.10) |\n|----------|------|----|---|---|----------------|\n| const | -0.8975 | 0.0400 | -22.43 | 0.0000 | — |\n| subject_acc_delta | 4.3928 | 1.3602 | 3.23 | 0.0012 | 1.552 |\n\n- Pseudo R² = 0.0007\n- AIC = 15545.2\n\n### Model 2: DIF_C ~ subject_acc_delta + ctt_difficulty + ctt_discrimination\n\n| Variable | Coef | SE | z | p |\n|----------|------|----|---|---|\n| const | 0.0691 | 0.0650 | 1.06 | 0.2877 |\n| subject_acc_delta | -3.0972 | 1.4305 | -2.17 | 0.0304 |\n| ctt_difficulty | -2.5435 | 0.1151 | -22.09 | 0.0000 |\n| ctt_discrimination | 4.1155 | 0.1929 | 21.33 | 0.0000 |\n\n- Pseudo R² = 0.0423\n- AIC = 14902.3\n\n## Counterfactual Analysis\n\n| Metric | Model 1 | Model 2 |\n|--------|---------|---------|\n| Predicted C% (actual) | 31.3% | 31.3% |\n| Predicted C% (Δ=0) | 29.0% | 33.0% |\n| Reduction | 2.4 pp | -1.6 pp |\n| % of C explained | 7.6% | -5.3% |\n\n## Subject-Level Correlation\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| Pearson r | 0.338 (p = 0.0101) |\n| Spearman ρ | 0.307 (p = 0.0201) |\n\n![Subject Delta vs C%](fig_subject_delta_vs_cpct.png)\n\n## Decomposition Summary\n\n- **Total observed C%**: 31.3%\n- **Model 1 (unadjusted)**: Domain improvement accounts for 2.4 pp (7.6% of total)\n- **Model 2 (adjusted for item properties)**: Domain improvement accounts for -1.6 pp — coefficient reverses sign after controlling for difficulty and discrimination\n\n## Interpretation\n\nTwo findings emerge from this decomposition:\n\n**1. Subject-level capability improvement is a weak predictor of DIF C flags.** Model 1 (pseudo R² = 0.0007) shows a statistically significant but negligible relationship: subjects where 2024 models improved more do show slightly more DIF C items (OR = 1.55 per 10pp improvement, p = 0.0012). However, this explains only 2.4 pp of the 31.3% C rate.\n","numLines":80,"startLine":1,"totalLines":88}}}
