internlm-2 | 14 | `chargoddard/internlm2-20b-llama` |\n46\t| yi-1.5 | 14 | `01-ai/Yi-1.5-34B-32K` |\n47\t\n48\t## 2. Graduated De-duplication Sweep\n49\t\n50\tEach family is capped at K models (most representative first). A matched random\n51\tsubsample of the same total N serves as control for sample-size effects.\n52\t\n53\t| Cap K | N_ref | N_foc | N_total | C% | Random C% (mean±sd) | ρ(Δ_MH) |\n54\t|-------|-------|-------|---------|-----|---------------------|---------|\n55\t| 1 | 15 | 18 | 33 | 0.17% | 0.16% ± 0.17% | 0.239 |\n56\t| 3 | 43 | 49 | 92 | 5.46% | 10.77% ± 2.52% | 0.310 |\n57\t| 5 | 71 | 75 | 146 | 11.69% | 16.89% ± 1.99% | 0.438 |\n58\t| 10 | 131 | 130 | 261 | 22.71% | 26.82% ± 2.39% | 0.580 |\n59\t| 20 | 227 | 220 | 447 | 29.12% | 30.91% ± 3.18% | 0.655 |\n60\t| 50 | 404 | 390 | 794 | 27.54% | 31.64% ± 0.80% | 0.742 |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43ea3076-440c-4e48-9471-1c78687f25f0","uuid":"94d5e95a-f2a1-4bda-9f11-04f563cbc843","timestamp":"2026-05-21T09:07:48.801Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/plan_022/model_independence_report.md","content":"# Plan 022: Model Independence Sensitivity Analysis\n\n## Motivation\n\nMETABENCH's 5227 models include many fine-tune/merge variants of the same base model.\nThese non-independent observations could inflate MH test statistics, potentially\noverstating the 31.3% C-rate. We systematically vary the degree of de-duplication\nto test robustness, using matched random subsamples as controls to disentangle\nsample-size effects from genuine family-structure effects.\n\n## 1. Family Structure\n\n- 2023 cohort: 1080 models in 15 families\n- 2024 cohort: 807 models in 18 families\n\n### Top-10 Largest Families\n\n**2023 Cohort:**\n\n| Family | Models | Representative |\n|--------|--------|---------------|\n| mistral | 547 | `cookinai/OrcaHermes-Mistral-70B-miqu` |\n| llama-2 | 161 | `lodrick-the-lafted/Grafted-Llama2-2x70B` |\n| zephyr | 86 | `mayacinka/NeuralZephyr-Beagle-7B` |\n| yi | 72 | `kyujinpy/PlatYi-34B-Llama-Q` |\n| phi-2 | 60 | `prhegde/merge-aanaphi-phi2-orage-3b` |\n| openchat | 30 | `Eric111/NeuralBeagleOpenChat` |\n| vicuna | 29 | `lorinma/yi6B_Vicuna` |\n| qwen | 27 | `Qwen/Qwen-72B` |\n| falcon | 21 | `tiiuae/falcon-40b` |\n| openhermes | 16 | `openaccess-ai-collective/DPOpenHermes-11B` |\n\n**2024 Cohort:**\n\n| Family | Models | Representative |\n|--------|--------|---------------|\n| llama-3 | 315 | `tenyx/Llama3-TenyxChat-70B` |\n| mixtral | 120 | `cloudyu/Mixtral_34Bx2_MoE_60B` |\n| solar | 91 | `macadeliccc/Orca-SOLAR-4x10.7b` |\n| gemma | 72 | `tushar310/MisGemma-7B` |\n| qwen-1.5 | 69 | `Qwen/Qwen1.5-110B` |\n| gemma-2 | 36 | `KeyonZeng/lion-gemma-2b` |\n| deepseek | 24 | `deepseek-ai/deepseek-llm-67b-base` |\n| phi-3 | 20 | `Ba2han/Llama-Phi-3_DoRA` |\n| internlm-2 | 14 | `chargoddard/internlm2-20b-llama` |\n| yi-1.5 | 14 | `01-ai/Yi-1.5-34B-32K` |\n\n## 2. Graduated De-duplication Sweep\n\nEach family is capped at K models (most representative first). A matched random\nsubsample of the same total N serves as control for sample-size effects.\n\n| Cap K | N_ref | N_foc | N_total | C% | Random C% (mean±sd) | ρ(Δ_MH) |\n|-------|-------|-------|---------|-----|---------------------|---------|\n| 1 | 15 | 18 | 33 | 0.17% | 0.16% ± 0.17% | 0.239 |\n| 3 | 43 | 49 | 92 | 5.46% | 10.77% ± 2.52% | 0.310 |\n| 5 | 71 | 75 | 146 | 11.69% | 16.89% ± 1.99% | 0.438 |\n| 10 | 131 | 130 | 261 | 22.71% | 26.82% ± 2.39% | 0.580 |\n| 20 | 227 | 220 | 447 | 29.12% | 30.91% ± 3.18% | 0.655 |\n| 50 | 404 | 390 | 794 | 27.54% | 31.64% ± 0.80% | 0.742 |","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":148}}}
